{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal","id":830599,"title":"Presenting my Werewolf AP - The Seventh Seal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-15T16:39:53-08:00","id":830599,"title":"Presenting my Werewolf AP - The Seventh Seal","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Dear friends,<br /> <br /> I'd like to humbly submit this game, played between myself and my dear friend Mr. Shopping (whom you may recognize as the ST from Detroit Rock City <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?446663-Werewolf-The-Forsaken-quot-Detroit-Rock-City-quot\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...Rock-City-quot</a>), as an example of Werewolf 2nd ed, but with a number of changes and leftovers from 1st ed that I liked, such as the harmony system and certain aspects of the background story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...e-Seventh-Seal</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">This game takes place in January of 2015 in the Windy City, a year after interpack conflict in the city reduced the Forsaken's numbers. Increasingly insular behavior, a seedy and deceptive Shadow, and pressure from Anshega and Hosts that see opportunities on Lake Michigan's shoreline make Chicago a less-than-friendly place to be a lone wolf, let alone unaligned with either side in the eternal war between </span><i>Urdaga</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> and </span><i>Anshega</i><span style=\"color:#333333\">.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Mr. Shopping's character, the star of this game is Lilly-Jane White, a lone Ghost Wolf </span><i>Ithaeur</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> who has prospered at the University of Chicago and created a relatively safe, coveted territory all on her own. Otherwise known as the White-Witch, she is well-loved by spirits and popular with people on her campus...Despised by the wider Uratha world, especially the </span><i>Urdaga</i><span style=\"color:#333333\">. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T16:51:24-08:00","id":830606,"title":"","content":"What a coincidence, I just started reading it over there.<br /> <br /> Always good to see Werewolf Actual Plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T16:57:29-08:00","id":830607,"title":"","content":"How exciting! Thank you. I'm going to try and update it weekly and bring in more art, maybe share some more of the maps that I use for clarity's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:01:01-08:00","id":830611,"title":"","content":"That would be really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T19:29:15-08:00","id":830704,"title":"","content":"Interesting to see how the characters turn out! Always nice to see what you and Mr. Shopping write Visk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T23:11:36-08:00","id":830857,"title":"","content":"Thank you Aynie! Just finished up with some major worky crap, going back home to USA now, so we've had some time to make something happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:48:42-08:00","id":830989,"title":"","content":"Well, what a compelling read. Pangur is a thing of brilliance. Kudos to you and Mr. Shopping, viskarenvisla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:40:15-08:00","id":831017,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love the idea of Spirit Claimed Golems, genius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:01:27-08:00","id":831330,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I am moved. Thank you all so much for your kind words. Honestly after the epic that was Detroit Rock City I was a little reluctant about putting my own AP up on the internet. Let us watch as Mr. Shopping prowls ever further into this world of unraveling darkness and fires in the cold...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:12:01-08:00","id":832342,"title":"","content":"I wanted to leave you guys with something to look at, possibly to help you with your own gaming if you haven't used it.<br /> <br /> I tend to use google maps to create environments, mark territories, and store information for my characters to check on missions. I got my inspiration from this from a variety of video games like, like Assassin's Creed, Shadows of Mordor, The Witcher 3, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zDwue5mYsjqg.kOX8Pm_OhQto&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zDwue5mYsjqg.kOX8Pm_OhQto&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zDwue5mYsjqg.kOX8Pm_OhQto&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zDwue5mYsjqg.kOX8Pm_OhQto&amp;usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T09:41:30-08:00","id":836486,"title":"","content":"Your Danny character is pretty intriguing, hope to learn more about him and hope he grows into something greater. I remember Mr. Shopping saying in the Detroit Rock City game there was a &quot;hidden&quot; loyalty mechanic for NPCs, when it got to a certain level, it would unlock certain bonuses pertaining to that NPC. Has that feature been kept for Seventh Seal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T00:53:07-08:00","id":836905,"title":"","content":"Doctor Crimson,<br /> <br /> I'm glad you like Danny. I had a moment of inspiration when I came up with him, and I'm glad that he gets to appear in Seventh Seal.<br /> <br /> As for the loyalty mechanic, yes, it's definitely there. Of course, LJ, as you've seen, is not very fond of other wolves, which means that those who partner up with her are likely either going to be unusual ghost wolves (perhaps like Danny), Wolfbloods, other creatures of the night, or spirits. The loyalty mechanic comes into effect for those who actually end up as her 'pack' for lack of a better term...if she succeeds.<br /> <br /> As for Danny's background? I'm curious myself if LJ will learn more about it. She already has a lot on her plate as a lone wolf, even with all her spirit buddies' support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T18:45:51-08:00","id":837854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=836905#post836905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doctor Crimson,<br /> <br /> I'm glad you like Danny. I had a moment of inspiration when I came up with him, and I'm glad that he gets to appear in Seventh Seal.<br /> <br /> As for the loyalty mechanic, yes, it's definitely there. Of course, LJ, as you've seen, is not very fond of other wolves, which means that those who partner up with her are likely either going to be unusual ghost wolves (perhaps like Danny), Wolfbloods, other creatures of the night, or spirits. The loyalty mechanic comes into effect for those who actually end up as her 'pack' for lack of a better term...if she succeeds.<br /> <br /> As for Danny's background? I'm curious myself if LJ will learn more about it. She already has a lot on her plate as a lone wolf, even with all her spirit buddies' support.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Completely bizarre to see Danny again. Do I get to roll to resist Death Rage if he hits on LJ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T01:58:00-08:00","id":837981,"title":"","content":"Dearest Aynie,<br /> <br /> Haha, not to worry -too- much. LJ really despises other wolves for the most part and finds the idea of a relationship with one revolting - you might remember that guy from the intro story, Bryan. An ill-fated love attempt from an Iron Master, complete with white roses and music, ending only in silver gunfire and disgrace.<br /> <br /> No, you'll Deathrage for other reasons :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T13:14:18-08:00","id":838772,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing I've missed in your other APs was that there was so much running around to different places that it was really hard to get a strong sense of the whole &quot;this is my domain and I'm going to protect it with my life&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> So I love LJ and the University so much. Very very awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T04:46:16-08:00","id":839065,"title":"","content":"----------<img src=\"http://img1.imagehousing.com/61/2c16a38a71fb1d3fadf515c803c83bd4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","user":"Mr. Shopping","date":". 02-29-2016, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","name":"Mr. Shopping","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T04:49:51-08:00","id":839066,"title":"","content":"Dear Errol,<br /> <br /> Thanks! Mr. Shopping will be really happy to hear that, LJ is quite enamored with her little mystical fortress of knowledge.<br /> <br /> One thing that's been fun about running this campaign in a specific, focused location, rather than the sort of heated, epic journeys of Shopping's games, is seeing how the specific place that LJ maintains affects her spirit friends, who have been a very fun part of the game for me to ST. <br /> <br /> Actually the Shadow has always been one of my biggest gripes with Werewolf, and I've always said that if I ever got around to rewriting it I'd remove the Shadow entirely and focus the game on fleshly matters. One reason I didn't like it because I really just had a hard time liking spirits and thinking of them as beings you can have relationships with, so I tried to take the time with LJ to rectify that. As you can see, some of her closest relationships are with spirits now - Pangur, Git &amp; Gat, Iffa, the Matriarch of the Library, Friend, and these have all been a challenge for me. I wanted them to be believable and relatable, but if you over humanize them, they don't feel like spirits. The middle ground has been the City Spirits, beings of my own invention.<br /> <br /> The Hisil is supposed to lack Human Spirits, so instead there are beings that reflect the activities and societies of the humans in their cities - as you've seen, Chicago's are dun colored, multiple-limbed sort of Gray Alien looking things. In Miami they look like Sahuagin, and in Seattle they almost all cover their faces and heads with hoods of some sort. Git, Gat, and Blue, being these types of spirits, have become some of my favorite NPCs to play.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned. Mr. Shopping and I just completed a certain intense confrontation, which I'll post soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T17:09:47-07:00","id":848490,"title":"","content":"Just updated the game - please have a look if you'd like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:50:21-07:00","id":849377,"title":"","content":"Been following along as you've been updating, and I remain utterly hooked. Keep up the fantastic work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/704-edge","name":"Edge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar704_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:43:49-07:00","id":856433,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to say that I'm still following along with this and enjoying it immensely. Are you writing this up as you play along or is the game completed and you are transcribing the logs after the fact?<br /> <br /> In a somewhat related note, I had a weird dream last night where Damien Wolfhound was going to horribly murder me and my family until we challenged him to Guitar Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:39:58-07:00","id":856498,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your praise, I'm very pleased you're enjoying this game. More updates to come soon, likely today or tomorrow!<br /> <br /> I'm writing this up as I play. The game hasn't been completed yet. I'd say we're maybe four or five sessions ahead of the actual place where I posted...maybe more, it's hard to say, but I certainly have more to post. <br /> <br /> As for your dream, that sounds really awful but I'm glad that Shopping made such a strong impression on your mind. I wonder if you'll start having nightmares about Wendigos after reading Seventh Seal :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:37:35-07:00","id":860026,"title":"","content":"Updated again - we're reaching the big battle between the Whispers and LJ. Wonder what'll happen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:58:51-07:00","id":861273,"title":"","content":"Wow, this is awesome. I've only just started reading, but I'm having a hard time wrapping my brain around why the Spirits like LJ but disdain the other Forsaken, or how she arose to this position of power. I think I'm only 3 or 4 posts deep, so I'm not certain if it gets clarified later, but I'd love to get some sense of what makes the White Witch the one in charge of this court of spirits.<br /> <br /> It's really cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:05:44-07:00","id":861770,"title":"","content":"Thanks Leetsepeak!<br /> <br /> You have a ways to go - that stuff will be covered later on at the end of Chapter 1. Thank you for taking the time to read.<br /> <br /> A couple things to keep in mind - these spirits are on LJ's side, and have the same notions of who's friend and who's foe. LJ despises the Forsaken, only aggravating the normal hostility most spirits have toward Urdaga, who are often seen as bossy and hypocritical. It's the Forsaken who tell the denizens of the Hisil that they're not allowed to ride humans, form cults, and generally be naughty - a role that was once fulfilled by a glorious terrifying God, not his rabble bastard offspring's offspring with an alien.<br /> <br /> I admit, it's been fun playing from a non-Forsaken perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:07:06-07:00","id":861772,"title":"","content":"-----------<br /> <img src=\"http://i63.tinypic.com/2udw1fp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","user":"Mr. Shopping","date":". 04-08-2016, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","name":"Mr. Shopping","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T20:30:40-07:00","id":866232,"title":"","content":"Ladies and gentlemen and all beyond and between,<br /> <br /> The log has been updated and the battle has been posted, with its aftermath - concluding Chapter 1. For those of you who have read this far, I hope you enjoyed it and are looking forward to Chapter 2, which is already being written - for those of you who haven't started already, I've tried to keep from adding too many spoilers, and I hope this humble game is worth a moment of your time to read.<br /> <br /> Stay turned for more Werewolf the Forsaken: The Seventh Seal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T08:41:45-07:00","id":866395,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i64.tinypic.com/2gv24o8.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Palatino Linotype\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b>All About Yours Truly</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Okay, fuck. Here goes.<br /> <br /> I don't even know why I'm writing this. If anyone besides me ever reads it, it means either I'm dead or I majorly fucked up. Or I actually found someone who I trust enough that I can share this with. Whatever, I'll probably burn this shit after I'm done. The point is to get it out and clear my freaking head so I can get on with my life.<br /> <br /> [There's a bunch of stylized doodles filling the upper right margin reminiscent of tattoo art or graffiti. Smoke. Demons. Marijuana. A white cartoon cat wearing an oversized beanie. She's clearly a talented artist.]<br /> <br /> So. Me. Um...Complicated.<br /> <br /> [A detailed and vibrant sketch of a pretty young woman in repose. Definitely some serious artistic talent here. The chick's bladed white bangs and locks of hair frame her face from under a navy blue University of Chicago beanie. Her body's athletic and toned, but svelte almost to the point of being skinny. She's dressed like a punker, and owns it with a kind of fierceness that's equal parts attitude and confidence. But the drawing somehow also effortlessly captures her easygoing nature - there's a lot of warmth and friendliness in her expression; that mysterious smile. Her black-lined eyes are dark, though, and incredibly intense - like she knows a lot more than anyone her age should. There's also a doodle of an ethereal, vaguely feline wisp resting on her knee.]<br /> <br /> The only people who still call me Lilly-Jane White all live in Steer Creek, Colorado. You won't find it on a map; it's basically a road, some trailer parks, a diner, and, like, a gas station. Population 200. That fucking place is what you think about when you hear Sweet Home Alabama. It's the kind of dump that Eminem raps about. It's like District 12 with Honey Boo Boo. Missing teeth. Creationism. Dumbing down. Poverty. Pregnant teens.<br /> <br /> Praise Jesus.<br /> <br /> You get the picture.<br /> <br /> Steer Creek. A microcosm of small town rednecks in a world totally in danger of being overrun by civilization. People there actually talk with rural-ass trailer trash accents. Steer Creek is the quintessential shit hole American town. Even thinking about it pisses me off.<br /> <br /> [A very unflattering sketch of a collection of dilapidated trailers. It's populated by Neanderthal-looking creatures in redneck garb. There's a nuclear explosion drawn nearby, detonating in a fireball that's about to gleefully wash over the encampment. There's a scrawl in the margin that says 'fuck Steer Creek' and 'BOOM'. ]<br /> <br /> FYI - I was born there. That awesome fact still ashames the hell out of me.<br /> <br /> My momma's name is Darla-May White. She's, I guess, a pretty good example of a small town single working mother. I think momma's worked at Rover's Diner waitressing like, her entire life, since back in the late 70s when it was called Horseshoe or some shit. She never finished high school, like 80% of the people there. She's kind, hardworking, and pretty sassy when she wants to be, and, like, as much as I hate to admit it, a really good cook. Momma has her moments too. We used to fight a lot, but I still love her. She's a protective, caring woman, as long as she's not drunk.<br /> <br /> Wow. That sounds pretty bad. And you know what? It <i>is</i>. She's got a fucking drinking problem, and it's probably because my dad left her soon as he found out she was pregnant. She's bounced around between deadbeat boyfriends ever since then. Momma said that my dad was the only man she ever loved, but obviously the fucker didn't deserve it. You read stories and see stuff on TV about abandoned kids trying to find their birth parents, but like, my dad? He's dead to me. Maybe he <i>is</i> dead. I don't know shit about him and I don't care to.<br /> <br /> Yeah. As far as I'm concerned, I was immaculate conception. Midi-chlorians and shit.<br /> <br /> [A sketch done American Gothic style with Darla in a waitressing uniform and a trailer behind, the husband's faceless face scratched out with an angry pen.]<br /> <br /> I was different than other kids in Steer Creek. Like, when I was really little, way before kindergarten, I started reading by myself. Most girls my age were into dolls but I was into books and magazines. My cousin, Daisy Blue Rain Gray (yes, I fucking know what you're thinking) always used to come over with her Barbies while our moms bitched in the next room. I'd read comics while she talked about how she was gonna be a wife one day and 'that's what girls like us do cuz boys iz expectin' it and daddy 'sez it's what God wants'. She got knocked up at 15, by the way. I think she has three or four kids now. Different fathers.<br /> <br /> I guess I started getting a better awareness of the world early on, like I was poor, and lived with people who were going nowhere, and there was so much more out there. I loved all the fairy tales and adventures in my books - y'know, pretending I was one of the characters out there doing extraordinary shit. Being incredible. Not a part of Steer Creek.<br /> <br /> In elementary I was first in every class by a huge margin. Gifted. Genius IQ and stuff. If it sounds like I'm bragging, sorry. I'm really not. The teachers wanted to send me to a special school but my mom didn't have the money. So I stayed and got bored with all the lessons, kind of dying a little every day stuck in class.<br /> It was alienating as fuck. I was the smart one, the smart aleck, smart-ass little Lilly-Jane who was better than everyone else. I was a fucking rebel, I guess, and eventually I just owned it in a town where being different was unthinkable. The only thing I had in common with them was this goddamn Steer Creek twang in my accent.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I'd go down by the old railroad tracks by the woods and pretend I was going Hemmingway and catching a train to somewhere I belonged. Sad, right?<br /> <br /> I don't know when exactly, but right around when I was 9 I started seeing shit.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah. This is the part where my story gets real. Weird. Please bear with me, and like, please don't judge. If you can do that, we can be best friends. For reals.<br /> <br /> I saw things no kid should ever see. Ghosts. Monsters. Angels. Demons. Spirits.<br /> <br /> The first couple times it happened, I wouldn't stop screaming - I think I woke up everyone in the trailer park when I saw this huge black shape outside my window crawling over the ground, creeping from home to home. Thinking back, it was probably a nighty-gaff, like a harmless fucker for the most part, but to a little girl, it looked like a demon. I saw other things too, both beautiful and freaking terrifying. Sometimes the future, sometimes the past. Sometimes shit that didn't make sense at all.<br /> <br /> For months it was ruining my life. The worst was when the things realized I could see them. They\u2019d beg. Threaten. Scream silently across an invisible barrier. I couldn't tell my momma or anyone. They'd think I was crazy - and maybe I was. I didn't know what was wrong with me, like, I went through the whole 'it's not real' to 'you've got brain cancer' to finally something between 'you're psychic' and 'you're psychotic'. Like in the comics I read, I wished it just meant I was a superhero or something, like the X-men. Or there was some fucking reason to it all.<br /> <br /> On the best days, I thought I was special. On the worst ones, I wanted to die.<br /> <br /> [An artistic sketch of strange, ghostly spirits, some nightmarish, some friendly, all swirling around and above a frightened-looking girl with dark hair, a much younger version of LJ.]<br /> <br /> Eventually I just started ignoring them, like, tuning them out as best I could. Going on with my life. Maybe you know what I'm talking about. Maybe you don't have a fucking clue. It would be years until I actually figured that shit out, but even now, not really. What I do know is that the stuff I was seeing made life in Steer Creek even harder for me.<br /> <br /> Nobody understood me. I dressed different, listened to different music. Didn't really have any friends. So I just kind of did my thing, had goddamn bibles beaten at me, went to school, got into mechanical stuff in my uncle's workshop shed, taking things apart and putting it back together - like basically one of the few extracurriculars that kept me sane.<br /> <br /> When I was in my early teens, I stopped seeing things as much. I don't know what it was, or why, but I could control it better. It was all about focus.<br /> <br /> My grades were good enough to get into Jefferson McLaughlin State Charter School in Denver and the Denver School of the Arts, but it was too far away and I sure as hell couldn't afford my own place. I had to settle for Arapahoe High. In case you're wondering, I could have gotten into any freaking private school in the country, but - you guessed it. Too poor.<br /> <br /> Aurora was the big city by comparison, and I had to drive out there every day in my uncle's busted-ass pickup to make my classes. But I had friends there. I had a real life there. I could be myself there and it was cool. At Arapahoe, I was LJ. Me. The smart-ass punker everyone liked.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, though, the visions got worse and made my life hell.<br /> <br /> It would have been so easy to drop out. If you went through what I went through, you wouldn't have blamed me - but being smart and doing well in school was the one thing that I knew made me better than Steer Creek and my fucked-up family.<br /> <br /> [An optimistic sketch of teenage LJ, a punker with punker friends, smoking weed, chilling, laughing on school steps. Gangster chick butterflies fly above.]<br /> <br /> Like I said, Steer Creek was a fucking black hole. Barely anyone there had ever made it out of Blackwood County. You were born there, you died there. But I'd found a way out. I worked my ass off in high school and aced my SATs. Top of my class and shit. Woo! I wanted to go somewhere as far away from my old life as possible, so I applied to Chicago, New York, Boston. I got into a lot of schools, big Ivies included, but I only got a full ride to UC, so, Chicago it was.<br /> <br /> College was a big fucking deal in my family, obviously because no one had been there. Most Steer Creek teens my age had already dropped out and were busy being baby mommies or working shit jobs up in Littleton or wherever. But momma and the others didn't want me to go. Either they were real proud, or real jealous, like most of my cousins. It ended predictably, with a huge fucking falling out with momma and the rest because I refused to go to CU-Boulder or Colorado State just because they were closer to the trailer park.<br /> <br /> A lot of really ugly shit I'd been holding in over the years finally came out. I said a lot of things that I probably shouldn't have said. Yelling. Screaming. Trailer park drama. Broken bottles, upended furniture. I ended up just taking my shit to my uncle's truck and driving to Chicago that night.<br /> <br /> [A sketch that fills up most of the page with an angry-looking punker LJ with dark hair and a beanie behind the wheel of a beat-up old pickup, a trailer park in flames behind her. The scene transitions to the skyscrapers of Chicago ahead. There's also a sketch of a zombie astronaut for some reason.]<br /> I slept in the truck the first couple of nights before I finally convinced the university to let me into a dorm early. After that? Freedom. A beautiful new city. It was like Aurora times a billion. I was finally my own person, and I could finally, like, really shine. It was my dream coming true.<br /> <br /> I didn't want anyone knowing where I came from. I, like, actively worked on killing my accent and totally embraced everything Chicago. I wasn't Lilly-Jane anymore. I was Lilith White. But mostly just LJ.<br /> <br /> When I was a froshie I made a lot of friends. So many people were like me and liked me. I was popular. It was insane. It was awesome. I was happy. Correction. Am happy.<br /> <br /> [A sketch of the UC campus, a dark-haired LJ held up on people's shoulders. Smiles, cheers. There's also a bunch of robots clapping in the background with flowers or something.]<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wish the story just ended there. Like, happily ever after, small town trailer trash chick goes to the big city and realizes her potential. Does something great with her life. Shots all around. Disney ending.<br /> Roll credits.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's kind of what happened. But it gets a lot darker first. If you believed the seeing shit part, or you're <i>in the know</i>, maybe you'll get what happened next.<br /> <br /> ['I do not want to talk about this', 'I'm sad', and 'I do not want to be here' is scribbled in the margins a few times. There's a sketch of a crescent moon illuminating a field full of dead werewolves in the Gauru. It's really graphic. One disemboweled, one dismembered. Part of it's been scribbled over. The next few lines of the letter are filled with crossed out words, like she's started and stopped writing several times. Some of the ink is different too, indicating that LJ put this away for a while and started again later. When it does resume, the words are deeply scratched into the paper.]<br /> <br /> I guess the whole point of this has been for me to write about this part. I don't really want to do details. I'm not ready but\u2026I\u2019ll try.<br /> <br /> Basically right at the end of my second semester freshman year, it got real hot. I remember that. It was fucking hot - maybe that's what triggered it; I don't know. I started seeing things again that no one else could see. Worse than ever. This time, <i>all</i> of them could see me. And this time, I could hear them too. Sometimes I could even feel them.<br /> <br /> Really, really weird shit started happening to me, like to my body. My senses. I was changing somehow and I was fucking terrified. But I did like what I did before, like, just school. Got high. Tried to ignore it.<br /> <br /> That was about when I met some real monsters. Like actual, legitimate, <i>evil </i>fucking monsters. They were a Chicago gang that looked like they were people, but...they weren't.<br /> <br /> The first time they came was when I was hanging out at this MDK concert, trying to forget what was happening and this creepy chick came up to me, all smirky and condescending as fuck. Something just felt wrong with her, like subtle things, like...the way she walked, the way she carried herself, how she looked at me, the way she felt...even now it's hard to explain that shit. She just made me feel really cold - like, she looked like a normal person on the outside but she was really, really scary.<br /> <br /> I don't want to describe her more. Sometimes I still see her face when I close my eyes; her face, along with the others. All of them. Sometimes in my nightmares too.<br /> <br /> This bitch tried to pull off this Trinity routine on me, like, everyone else was sheep and only some of us could be wolves in this world - she could show me the truth, like show me my destiny, make me worth something. Said her name was Jessie, and I needed to come with her.<br /> <br /> I seriously thought she was on drugs. Part of a cult.<br /> <br /> I guess it turns out the cult part was kinda true, right? But whatever.<br /> <br /> I remember I told her to fuck herself and leave me alone. Big middle finger right in her face. A good dose of LJ attitude. If I knew what I know now, I would've ran. Like got the fuck out of the state, just like as far away as possible.<br /> <br /> No. Fuck that. I would've gotten a silver knife and buried it into Jessie's FUCKING eye socket.<br /> <br /> After that night, I started feeling like I was being watched, like, followed. It came along with everything else, all the crazy shit I was seeing and experiencing, but now I know they were stalking me, like, <i>hunting </i>me.<br /> <br /> A couple of nights later, they came out into the open. I was walking back to my dorm from The Lair with some Chicago friends. We were supposed to go to Oak Street Beach the next day. Never happened. That was the first time I met Ben Tarn. Big scary fucker, trenchcoat, dirty beard, came out of nowhere. He let Nova and Harley run when he slid out this long knife, but not me. It was horror movie chick perfect, me running scared, right into the backstreets and alleys, all of them empty. Eerie as hell. I try to get back to the main street? He was always there. And if I turned down the wrong alley? A real live fucking wolf was there, teeth bared, warning me to turn back.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re in the know, you\u2019ll know this is standard shit, Forsaken terror tactics. You\u2019ve probably heard it before. Maybe you were a victim. Maybe you were part of it - if you were - <u>FUCK</u> you.<br /> <br /> They herded me into a dead end where I met the rest of their whole monster \u201cfamily\u201d. They were standing around some fucking barrel fire, trying to look all dramatic. Predatory street thugs.<br /> <br /> This asshole Amal, their leader, who thought he was slick shit, like always the smartest guy in the room. Jessie, of course, who was looking smug as hell. Major fucking bitch. Some sick dickhead named Tanner too. And then there was Ben, who was right behind me, blocking the way with his fucking knife. Behind him? That lanky, freaky wolf, snarling and bristling, coming right up to his side. That was so crazy to me, like a gang I could get, but an actual wolf with them?<br /> <br /> It was all designed to intimidate me, like I was a scared, stupid kid and bring me into the fold. Help me \u201crealize my destiny\u201d - that shit again. Amal was a smooth-talking, evil fuckface who gave me the expanded version of the same crap that Jessie was trying to feed me at MDK. He told me they\u2019d been watching me real close - he used my name, like that meant he knew everything about me. He said it was time for me to hear some hard truths.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe world isn\u2019t what you think, Lilly-Jane,\u201d he\u2019d said. \u201cAnd you\u2019re a truly special little girl. Don\u2019t you have questions about yourself? Why you\u2019re different than everyone else?\u201d<br /> <br /> I told him to fuck himself and to leave me the hell alone. I was scared, but that fear was turning to anger.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow that\u2019s no way to show your gratitude, Ms. White,\u201d Amal had said, while the others just stared at me. Not like people. Like wolves. \u201cWe\u2019ve been running damage control on you for weeks. Making sure you didn\u2019t hurt anyone or cause any more trouble than you already have.\u201d<br /> <br /> When I turned to try to run again, that wolf at big Ben Tarn\u2019s side did the impossible - she stood up and changed. Her body shifted and grew, fur disappeared to street clothes, and while I was freaking the fuck out, this girl who looked about my age stood there where the wolf had been before. I found out later this was Amal\u2019s sister, Anitra, a real sadistic fucking cunt. She came forwards and pushed me, like threw me five feet up against the wall and I just crashed to the ground. The bitch stood over me, gloating, and told me that I was in their world now.<br /> <br /> She went over to stand next to Amal and told me that the university, my life, how I was such a rebel against authority - like obviously based on their stalker observations and nothing else - all of it was over now. It was bullshit and -they- were the only thing that mattered - their family. They were going to make my life mean something. So come with them. Don\u2019t make it hard on myself. There was this wild, totally inhuman look in her eyes - fuck, her eyes weren\u2019t even a person\u2019s. Everything had changed from wolf to human except them.<br /> <br /> I never really hated anyone like I hated the five of them. I\u2019m a pretty good judge of character, and these people were bad. Like evil. True monsters.<br /> <br /> Watching Anitra change in front of me like that, it\u2019s hard for me to describe. Seeing things my whole life was bad enough, but it was like all of it was spilling into the real world. I couldn\u2019t just focus it away anymore and it freaked the hell out of me. I was shaking when I got up and Amal started talking about how I belonged to them now and my new life or some BS - I wasn\u2019t listening. I just had to get the fuck out of there and away from them.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think they were expecting me to fight back. Maybe they thought I was too scared, or weak, but when I tried to run that time, I went straight for Ben\u2019s knife instead. He sure as hell didn\u2019t think I\u2019d try anything like that, like tackling him with my whole body. Stupid, maybe, but I\u2019d taken self-defense classes and some kickboxing too, so I knew how to handle myself in a fight. All I had to do was grab that knife and push - it went right into his guts. When the pain came out of his mouth, he didn\u2019t sound human at all. His face started rippling under the surface - fucking hideous. But I was already running fast as I could towards the main street and screaming for help.<br /> <br /> They probably let me get away. Anitra, Tanner and Jessie were real close behind, but I came out onto the middle a busy street, shrieking and attracting all kinds of attention\u2026they just stopped at the mouth of the alley as cars starting screeching to a halt all around. They looked at each other, then me, and just kind of slunk back into the shadows.<br /> <br /> I was crying and gasping for breath. People, actual good Samaritans, came over to help me. I said some gang in the alley was after me, tried to kidnap me. They called the cops, and I went and made a statement. Pointless, right? But I was really scared and I didn\u2019t know what else to do. I spent the night at the station sleeping on this couch because I didn\u2019t feel safe in the dorm. The police couldn\u2019t do much else.<br /> <br /> The next day the cops gave me a lift back to UC. I was paranoid as fuck, just like, tried to stay in public places where there were lots of people. The monsters didn\u2019t want to be seen by people, I got that, so that was the only way I\u2019d be safe, unless I wanted to, like, live in the fucking police station.<br /> <br /> I had this shady friend named Zay who hooked me up with pot and stuff, so I did my 2nd Amendment thing and got myself a gun that afternoon. I mean, what would you do? I knew how to shoot - I used to snipe bottles and boards with Uncle Roy\u2019s .38 back in Steer Creek in my early teens and, like, any time I had to come back from Aurora. Probably the only useful life skill I picked up out there.<br /> <br /> Things would\u2019ve been a lot different if I\u2019d loaded that iron up with silver bullets. That\u2019s what I pack now, right? You better fucking believe it, dude. But back then, I just couldn\u2019t put two and two together. Nobody in my situation could.<br /> <br /> So I was carrying. It gave me some of my confidence back but I was still \u2018noided out by every fucking bump and boo. I knew that they were watching me, somehow. Visions getting worse, you know, like<br /> <br /> [The text drifts off into a picture of Lilith sitting alone in the dark, holding a handgun down between her legs, head bowed, eyes shadowed under dark bangs and her beanie. Behind her is a fractal world, a miasma of dream and nightmare, real and supernatural. And in the dark are the five wolves hunting her.]<br /> <br /> I was going to try to get out of town the next day, just like, leave the city for a while, maybe go back to Aurora to stay with a friend or maybe even Steer Creek. Anywhere but Chicago.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t sleep that night. Just like, lay awake on my bed. Smoked some pot and tried to chill out, but that gun was right next to me. It was late, like 2 AM or something but I was still wide awake, so when I heard the glass dorm security door just freaking shatter, I was up and out into the hall, but Ben Tarn was already on me. He knocked me down and said he\u2019d teach me a lesson. Guy didn\u2019t look human anymore at all - his nose and mouth were fused, his eyes all yellow and fucked up; some hideous mix of man and wolf. He had his knife out, like he was going to carve me up, but when he came in, he fucking -bit- me. Shoulder and neck. He wasn\u2019t expecting the gun though. When Ben came up, my blood all over his jagged, ugly-ass teeth, I started shooting. One went into the ceiling but one hit him in the face, right in one of his eyes. It knocked him back and onto the floor and made him make this horrible howling scream, but it wasn\u2019t enough to kill his ass.<br /> <br /> I guess I could\u2019ve kept shooting. Enough bullets to the head probably would\u2019ve put him down, but I didn\u2019t know that yet. I just wanted to get away. I thought maybe he <i>was</i> dead. I ran out into the night, through the streets, screaming, but nobody gave a shit this time. Empty campus, empty streets - and Ben Tarn was right behind me, bleeding from that empty, blown-out eye socket. Then he was a wolf, right at my heels. I realize now that he was chasing me into the woods, keeping just far away for me not to get a good shot, maybe letting me think I\u2019d have a chance to get away. But that\u2019s what Ben wanted all the long. Stupid. Stupid.<br /> <br /> I still remember the crunch when the bear trap went around my leg. Ben Tarn had set it, of course. He was their best hunter. I was screaming, on the ground, crying for help, for him to get away from me, leave me alone. Horror movie chick again.<br /> <br /> It was real bad. Any pretense of Ben being human was gone when he started stalking up to me and I emptied my revolver into his chest. Didn\u2019t stop him. After that, he just beat the hell out of me. I mean, just took it all out on me. The monster hated me. He broke bones, just\u2026I don\u2019t want to talk about it.<br /> <br /> When I woke up, I hurt all over, real bad, but not, like, I should have. Bones that I knew had been shattered weren\u2019t anymore. It was dark again. I heard the voices of my captors, the bastards from the alley. They\u2019d sat me up on the porch of this old farmhouse in the middle of nowhere, Illinois. Creepy cornfields. My ankle was shackled to the railing, and my clothes were bloodied. All five of them were out in the yard in front of me, a big bonfire roaring. Ben was wearing this eyepatch. That made me smile.<br /> <br /> Anitra came up to me with a washcloth and a bag of MacDonald\u2019s. Like that was going to make us sisters. She said she was my friend. I started screaming again, knocked that shit away and told them I wanted to go home, they were monsters; started yelling for help. Amal started trying to sell their poison to me again, but I wouldn\u2019t shut up.<br /> <br /> They were happy to hurt me. To teach me a lesson again. Anitra did it this time, said it was for my own good. I tried to fight back, but what the fuck can you do with a leg iron against someone who can turn into a man-wolf thing, head and shoulders bigger than you? I could see it in Anitra's eyes when she was kicking me when I was down - she enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> I decided to stay quiet then, tears streaming down my face. Just staring straight into the fire. Passive resistance. Amal kept doing his prostheletizing. I don\u2019t remember what else he said, except that they called themselves the Lightning Runners. I just tuned the rest out. He kept asking me questions, like, don\u2019t I want to know what\u2019s happening to me? Don\u2019t I want to know about my purpose and my power? Why my body was healing like this? But I didn\u2019t answer.<br /> <br /> Eventually he gave up for the evening after all he got was my stony silence. Each of them tried to talk sense into me that night. All except Ben. Tanner said they weren\u2019t bad people, and this wasn\u2019t easy for them - I laughed at that, which won me a kick in the throat. But that just vindicated me. Anitra, she said she knew punker bitches like me, and we were all posers, and I was just a scared little girl. I\u2019d have to work real hard to ever be good enough to be her sister, and she was losing hope. I spat up into Anitra\u2019s face and told her I\u2019d never be her fucking sister or join their fucking family. Yeah. Broke my nose for that.<br /> <br /> She\u2019dve done worse if Jessie hadn\u2019t caught her fist. The older wolf got down real low and looked at me with pity. I tried to plead with her for help but there wasn\u2019t any humanity there. Jessie just said I needed to accept this or I wouldn\u2019t make it. Ben already thought I was dangerous. Some of the ones like me, the ones that were too wild, they just died. Or they had to be put down, and I was starting to look like that. So I needed to make that choice, to choose family or choose death. They\u2019d take care of me. She was sorry that this\u2019d happened but I\u2019d brought it on myself.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t say shit. Just glared at her defiantly, like there was no way in hell.<br /> <br /> That night they partied for hours and got real drunk - probably celebrating the successful hunt. Anitra threw a beer at me; the bottle hit the wall behind and broke. She said I could lap that up if I was thirsty. I overheard Ben talking about how much he hated me. He\u2019d lost face for the knife thing and getting shot up by a teenage girl, but Amal said I was important and I\u2019d come around.<br /> <br /> Yeah. I\u2019d come around.<br /> <br /> That night I worked on the leg iron. The Lightning Runners had all gone to bed drunk and left me out there alone. The shackle was pretty heavy duty and they\u2019d put it on my ankle real tight. The damage they\u2019d inflicted on me slowly started feeling better. I didn\u2019t know why but it didn\u2019t matter as much as escape. I wasn\u2019t strong enough to break the chain, or the metal railing it was attached to, but the wooden top that ran across? I slowly, painstakingly got the rail free by using the chain to saw through the wood until it was weak enough for me to finally just barely pop it out. Took hours, and my hands were raw, but I did it.<br /> <br /> I had no idea where the fuck I was. There were a couple of cars parked out front, but none of them had keys in them. I sure as hell wasn\u2019t going into the house to try and find them, dragging this rattling chain behind me. I was terrified that someone might wake up and find me. If I ran down the road, I might find a car, but Ben Tarn might find me first. The fire was real low - flickers and embers - but still enough for me to get some burning planks out though. I set fire to the porch and threw some up onto the roof. The farmhouse was old wood, so it caught fire fast. Really fast.<br /> <br /> Great distraction. I burned the whole fucker down, but they caught me anyway. I didn\u2019t get out of the back roads before the Lightning Runners ran me down, all wolves this time.<br /> <br /> Sooo\u2026we finally get to the part I really don\u2019t like talking about. We all have demons, right? Stuff we\u2019ve done or done to us that we try to bury down deep. Or forget. Or say never happened. This one\u2019s mine.<br /> <br /> I got caught by the monsters and they really went to town on me for torching their clubhouse. Some of them got burned real bad too. So they showed me their true nature.<br /> <br /> Biting me, tearing at me and my clothes. Torn flesh, my blood all over. Tugging me in-between their teeth. It\u2019s all a jumble, really. It felt like it wasn\u2019t really happening to me but happening to someone else. Out-of-body. I thought I was going to die.<br /> <br /> When I woke up again, I was down in a hole. It was a big old storm drain - evil as hell, that place, big tunnel on either side, barred off by heavy grates so I couldn\u2019t run. Up top, the only light came from a square grate fifteen feet up. They\u2019d stripped off all my clothes in an attempt to humiliate me and take away my dignity. Anitra was assigned to be my tormentor and had the dubious honor of getting to break me. She\u2019d dump leftovers down the hole from what the pack ate and drank. Anitra taunted me from up above, sometimes dragging a board over it to plunge me into pitch black for what felt like days at a time. The visions got real worse then, when I was alone in the dark. It stank like hell.<br /> <br /> Anitra kept asking me if I was ready to be a good girl and come up and join the family, but all she got was me screaming shit up like her like I\u2019d kill them all, just let me go, I\u2019d die first. I didn\u2019t want to be a monster like them.<br /> <br /> The torture kept coming, physical and mental. When it rained and the drain got almost full, and I\u2019d be hanging on for dear life, swimming and gasping for breath against the top grate with a couple of inches of air between me and the water. Anitra promised all sorts of shit - a shower, fresh clothes, a toilet, real hot food.<br /> <br /> Weeks of this shit. It just got worse when I didn\u2019t break.<br /> <br /> You might be like, why didn\u2019t I just give in?<br /> <br /> I admit, it was unbelievably traumatizing. I\u2019m still fucked-up over it, but you need to know something about me, okay? I\u2019d fought so hard for my life in Chicago U, to be my own person, to be me and have my own life. I wasn\u2019t going to have anyone take it away and make me a monster. No shit, something was happening to me - all the beatings they\u2019d given me had faded. I could see it on myself. Just some scars from where they\u2019d savaged me as wolves. No way should any of that've gone away in a few days, but it did.<br /> <br /> Anitra got frustrated. She started dropping dead rats down instead of food. One night Tanner pissed down the hole. But the worst was when she caught some of my old Steek Creek accent coming through, and she said things to me that still hurt. Her and Tanner both. I can\u2019t believe how much I <i>still</i> fucking hate them.<br /> <br /> A couple weeks in, I finally told Anitra I was ready. It was easy to fake the tears, I was so fucked up. But when she put the ladder down to let me up, I went right for her neck and tried to choke the life out of her like a fucking psycho. Mistake, obviously.<br /> <br /> When I woke up this time, they had me all snared up in chicken wire down there, the shit digging into my throat and making it almost impossible to breathe. All five of them were up above discussing me when they thought I was out. It sounded like they desperately needed me for something. They called me Ithaeur. Tanner was saying that he didn\u2019t know if it was worth it. Ben was saying shit like I was dangerous, a lot more dangerous than I looked and keeping me would be bad. He didn\u2019t think I\u2019d break anymore. Jessie agreed I was dangerous, but still thought I could be on their side, a real asset. Amal agreed. Anitra was frustrated as hell. She thought I was a stupid bitch and I didn\u2019t know what was good for me. She wanted me dead too. But all that mattered was what Amal thought. He said there just too few of the People to wait for another Ithaeur, and they all knew what was at stake.<br /> <br /> I watched the moon change through the grate, and they left me down there for days without food or water. When Jessie finally came down to let me out of the wire, I was too weak to fight. Covered in dried blood and cuts from where the metal had dug into my skin. She brought me a pizza in a box and a big bottle of water but at the same time she put really heavy chains around my ankles, which made it nearly impossible for me to move much.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t say anything, just gave me this really concerned look at the way I was still glaring at her. Maybe she knew how much I wanted to kill them. Maybe she\u2019d realized her mistake.<br /> <br /> But that kindness didn\u2019t last. They only threw down raw meat after that - some of it rotten. Half-eaten animal carcasses. Like they were trying to make me less than human. I didn\u2019t want to die, but that whole thing\u2026it was a living nightmare, man, a hell I wouldn\u2019t wish on anyone but them.<br /> <br /> It didn't matter how hungry I was. I was crying, and I wanted to eat so badly, but I didn't.<br /> <br /> Ben Tarn dropped this deer skull down one night when the moon was waning, going down from half to crescent. Most of the meat was gone, sockets all empty, big broken antlers. I thought I\u2019d finally lost my mind when it started talking to me.<br /> <br /> The skull said it was my friend, and it was going to help me get free. It\u2019d help me get free and then kill the wolves that did this to me.<br /> <br /> They probably thought I\u2019d snapped when I started talking to it. It told me things, about what was really happening to me, and how when the crescent moon was full, it\u2019d be time. All I had to do was let him in. I believed him too. I don\u2019t know why, but Friend\u2019s never lied to me. He told me that I\u2019d get to live my life. I\u2019d get it back if I just let him in when it was time. I could use my power however I wanted, because it was mine. I didn\u2019t have to be afraid. I felt warmth when I held the skull, like a blanket around me. I felt concern. I felt love, as alien as it was.<br /> <br /> [There\u2019s a sketch of the stag skull in the margin, eyes like coals burning in the sockets. Some words, mostly illegible are in the margin - \u2018I love Friend\u2019 and \u2018I owe Friend my life\u2019 are about all you can make out.]<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t matter what they did to me after that. I just laughed. It freaked the hell out of Anitra. I just told them they\u2019d all be dead soon.<br /> <br /> When the crescent moon was full that final night, I started hearing this otherworldly song. Angelic, demonic, a shimmering woman\u2019s aria from far away. It overwhelmed my senses, and the moon shone down on me and ripped through me like<br /> <br /> [Words trail off.]<br /> <br /> I saw Friend in that moment, like for what he really was - this giant shape, this wendigo embodiment of terror, this whispering dark angel that wore the face of the dead stag. I opened my arms and let him in, and I screamed my soul out<br /> <br /> [Illegible.]<br /> <br /> He was in me and the power was like being a god, like nothing I ever felt before or ever since. I wasn\u2019t me anymore when I tore out of that fucking storm drain. I was this unstoppable thing, this killing machine. All I saw was red heat and blood. With Friend inside me, I made good on my promise to the Lightning Runners. We tore them apart. None of them had a chance. I saw fear in their eyes, heard their terror, and it just made Friend stronger. There was a lot of blood, and a lot of screaming. Some of them were able to become wolf-gods themselves, but it didn\u2019t matter. Friend did things through me - he made their claws and jaws do nothing. All their Shadow tricks failed. Some of them begged. It didn\u2019t matter. He tore their spirits out of their bodies.<br /> <br /> When it was done, I was naked and drenched in their blood and gore. Head to toe. Their body parts were all over the fucking woods. Trees smashed. I was gasping for breath but unhurt. Everything looked different - sharper, brighter. My senses were a thousand times what they\u2019d used to be. My body felt stronger, healthier.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d changed, but I was free. Friend was there, his presence over me, and all I could do was cry and thank him over and over again. He said he\u2019d come for me when I was ready, and then he was gone.<br /> <br /> I dragged what was left of the Lightning Runners and threw them down the storm drain where they belonged. I\u2019m not an evil person but I\u2019d never been so satisfied as to see the glassy fear in their dead fucking eyes as they disappeared down into the dark.<br /> <br /> Okay. Wow. Never thought I\u2019d write that down.<br /> <br /> So\u2026life goes on, right? They had a big shack nearby that was probably one of their safehouses. Took the best shower of my life, still shaking with adrenaline, and saw something else. My hair was now a shock of pure white, my brows black\u2026my eyes this intense, incredible violet. Friend being inside me during that first change, it\u2019d left its mark on my soul.<br /> <br /> I liked it.<br /> <br /> I took some of Anitra\u2019s clothes and eventually made it back to civilization and the University of Chicago. It was still summer vacation and nobody had really missed me. I just said I\u2019d been visiting family. My new look? I owned it. The break in? Some tweaker maniac running through campus with a gun. Police were still looking for him.<br /> <br /> Friend came to me a few nights later. He showed me how to cross over into the Hisil, the spirit world. He took me to his secret place in the dark forest and taught me everything, all without the Forsaken lies. He showed me the power in my spirit side and in my blood, and gave me gifts that no Uratha would ever have.<br /> <br /> So how\u2019d I become the White-Haired Witch? White hair\u2019s self-explanatory, but coming to rule the University\u2019s spiritside\u2019s not at all what you might think.<br /> <br /> It just\u2026kind of happened.<br /> <br /> Friend told me all the Father Wolf bullshit, about what the Forsaken thought their duty was.<br /> <br /> Yeah right. The spirits came to me for help and I helped them out. I didn't treat them like the Forsaken did, like they were prey. I let spirits do their thing, as long as no one back in the real world got hurt. That was a big deal to them. No one to control them, or police them. They saw me less like a predator and more like a friend.<br /> <br /> Spirits...they're like animals or children, like...they\u2019re pure and na\u00efve, y'know? They just need someone to help guide them, and I just\u2026kind of took that role. I became the University\u2019s de-facto guardian. Some said I was its queen, which made me uncomfortable at first, but when this court came into being just for me, who was I to refuse, especially if it helped me keep things safe for everyone? If there was one thing I could do, it would be to make sure none of my classmates ever had to go through what I did, so I made sure all the Uratha, all the things in the darkness knew that they couldn\u2019t come to UC and fuck around.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, one last thing. Pangur.<br /> <br /> I have the moon brands on my arm and up my shoulder but I\u2019m no moon-slave. I\u2019m no Forsaken. I\u2019ve got no love for the Lunes either, or that crazy bitch Luna. But they took an interest in me anyway. Maybe because of my bond with Friend, the Terror King. Or who knows why. But they sent someone to watch after me not long after I left Friend\u2019s dark forest.<br /> <br /> Pangur started out as this little ping-pong sized ball of silver light that came down on my window sill and hid in my backpack, manifesting himself in the Flesh. I tried to get it to fuck off but he stuck around no matter what I did. Eventually I tried communicating, but this glimmerling? All it could do was make these ding-ding chimey noises. Shiver when it was mad or scared. I let it hang around, watch TV with me. Y\u2019know. Like you do in your sophomore year.<br /> <br /> Over time, the glimmerling changed too. Like an infant, he started talking - hilariously, mimicking me. Laughing like a baby. Then he started making faces on the surface of his orb. One day, we were watching cute YouTube cats and Internet memes and he turned into this glowing, silvery kitten. Cutest fucking thing. Suddenly I had a kitty.<br /> <br /> He grew up with me as I raised him on a healthy diet of TV and Internet. Now I\u2019m a senior and he\u2019s like, I don\u2019t know, a young adolescent or something. My best friend in the whole world. I'm still not Forsaken, but that doesn't really matter to him.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s it. Werewolf memoir complete. I\u2019m doing good now, like well-adjusted, doing my whole walking between the two worlds thing while keeping up my 4.0 GPA. Valedictorian track, bitches. Go Maroons! Woo.<br /> <br /> [A Disney-style rendition of LJ and Pangur together with big smiles. Underneath: \u2018<b>YO MAMA!</b>\u2019]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/603-mr-shopping","name":"Mr. Shopping","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:39:51-07:00","id":866441,"title":"","content":"Once again, a joy to read, guys. I eagerly await Chapter 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/704-edge","name":"Edge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar704_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:31:31-07:00","id":866848,"title":"","content":"Brutal. Whispers never stood a chance. You've got me wondering though; what are Git and Gat's influences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:22:47-07:00","id":866988,"title":"","content":"I know you're using variant harmony/kuruth rules, but was there much of a danger of LJ flipping out and murdering her friends after her first change? In 2e a new wolf is basically a ticking time bomb depending on which triggers you pick. Maybe Friend's instruction was enough to avoid that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T00:11:52-07:00","id":868236,"title":"","content":"Hey there solidork,<br /> <br /> To answer your first question, Git and Gat have influences in 'Guns' and 'Urban', as do all City-Folk spirits. As for LJ twigging and murdering her friends after she'd changed, part of it is that the Lightning-Runners had taught her enough about how to control herself that it stuck, and she was also in the right place at the right time - curious, isn't it, that a single lone-wolf, even backed by a powerful spirit, should be able to control the University of Chicago without considerable competition.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Mr. Shopping would be glad to his input as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:52:58-07:00","id":877689,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;[Friend knows...Seven is the number of the fire that glows...]&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The beginning of chapter two has been posted. We shall play more tonight. Be'est thou aware!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T16:49:55-07:00","id":890249,"title":"","content":"More of chapter two to come, I just moved and am waiting for Internet installation. Stupid internet installation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:53:12-07:00","id":891941,"title":"","content":"Just caught up after some time away from my internet connection. Still loving it, guys. I just really hope that last Resolve + Composure roll wasn't for Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","user":"trivialrealities","date":". 05-16-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:53:22-07:00","id":894297,"title":"","content":"Hey Trivial,<br /> <br /> Thanks for the praise, makes my day during tough times without internet and only 3G.<br /> <br /> That last roll...well you'll find out when I get the next post up, which will probably be tomorrow. In the meantime let's talk kuruth for a bit!<br /> <br /> Kuruth is one of my favorite things about Werewolf. I like that they have tried to refine it, but again I strongly prefer to give my players a chance to avoid kuruth, even if presented with their trigger. <br /> <br /> LJ's trigger fits with her experiences - in addition to the normal parameters for death rage she will test if she is bound or captured in various scenarios. Being trapped in a room and locked up like a prison, being chained up, or at low levels of harmony even being grappled, will also trigger a test.<br /> <br /> Now I see Kuruth tests as taking place on a spectrum - failure doesn't always mean Wasu-Im, it can mean losing your shit in the Hishu, or lashing out at someone. Of course it can also mean buzzing straight off into berserker fury depending on the stimulus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T08:07:40-07:00","id":896820,"title":"","content":"More of the log has been posted. God help LJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:13:10-07:00","id":898936,"title":"","content":"Geez. It's almost as if Mother Moon has it out for her for some reason... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:45:22-07:00","id":909384,"title":"","content":"Updated yesterday, enjoy! <br /> <br /> Watch as events swirl and whirl about LJ - which can she handle? Which fall through her fingers? How much can a Lone Wolf handle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:12:07-07:00","id":911874,"title":"","content":"Well, LJ just can't catch a break.<br /> <br /> Also, can I ask how you set your game map up, viska? I'm running an online WtF game myself at the moment in my local city, but none of the players are familiar with it. A map like yours would be handy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:32:15-07:00","id":912025,"title":"","content":"Hey Trivial,<br /> <br /> The way you make a map on Google is you go to maps.google.com and choose &quot;My Places&quot;. Then you go to your city and start populating it with those points - there's one for fields, like the kind I use to mark territories, or points which can have different icons. I recommend using just the &quot;line&quot; option to mark your players' turf's border, that way it'll be easier to select and add icons - with the field option you can't easily select icons within the field. You'll see what I mean when you experiment.<br /> <br /> Maps like this make life easier I've found, which is why they're such an overused trope in videogames. I've even used alternative map programs to have a Fleshworld overlay and a Hisil overlay, marking out specific sections of Shadow as having different attributes or hosting different denizens. It requires a lot of work though lol<br /> <br /> Hope that helps! Feel free to ask other questions, I'll help as best I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:59:36-07:00","id":912053,"title":"","content":"Posted more - you'll get a look at one of the ways LJ gathers information to create rituals and cures from her Library.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T03:40:02-07:00","id":912181,"title":"","content":"LJ <i>really</i> cannot catch a break, can she? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And the tips on the map are great! Already worlds better than my crappy MSPaint borders on satellite images, and I've barely even started. So, thanks for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T04:05:22-07:00","id":912185,"title":"","content":"Nice, share the map with me when you're done. I wanna see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","user":"viskarenvisla","date":".  Wrong pronoun 06-12-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T12:41:26-07:00","id":912935,"title":"","content":"Since's viska gave me the all-clear to share it here as well, <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=14qyGHI1ZhQkB4eqqsfe5Sx7LNtQ\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> the map for the Skype game I'm running at the moment, Flesh By The Pound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T18:12:11-07:00","id":913120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trivialrealities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=912935#post912935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since's viska gave me the all-clear to share it here as well, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=14qyGHI1ZhQkB4eqqsfe5Sx7LNtQ&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> the map for the Skype game I'm running at the moment, Flesh By The Pound.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The concept behind The Invisible City pack is very compelling, very cool trivial. I get the feeling they may be playing with fire and even the Forsaken may be concerned by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:54:01-07:00","id":913267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doctor Crimson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=913120#post913120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The concept behind The Invisible City pack is very compelling, very cool trivial. I get the feeling they may be playing with fire and even the Forsaken may be concerned by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, I cannot take credit for them. Both they and Sky's Talons are from Shadows of the UK. Which, as a Brit, I do recommend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:15:53-07:00","id":914475,"title":"","content":"Here's a question for all of ye - in your games, are the only sources of Renown from Lunes and Anshega totems, or do you offer other means to gain it?<br /> <br /> I generally rule that spirits of Rank 7 and above can reward Renown to Werewolves - theoretically if some Uratha made an epic pact with Helios he could give Renown, but he hates Uratha for what they did to his sister's love and the sun, being an essentially immutable thing by nature, doesn't change its opinions easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:12:36-07:00","id":932948,"title":"","content":"Hey friends, we've been dealing with RL stuff lately but Seventh Seal is back on track. We just played last night, and soon I'll have more material to put up. Stay tuned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T10:18:14-07:00","id":932950,"title":"","content":"Good to hear! Eagerly looking forward to seeing what happens to LJ next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T15:10:24-07:00","id":943030,"title":"","content":"Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for your patience. I have posted the newest bits of Seventh Seal over at <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?775548-Werewolf-the-Forsaken-The-Seventh-Seal\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...e-Seventh-Seal</a> for your reading pleasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:55:50-07:00","id":944413,"title":"","content":"Well, at least nothing bad happened for LJ this time? Though I am concerned Honeybun might end up as a Promethean due to sheer chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:56:30-07:00","id":955353,"title":"","content":"More has been posted - I wonder what shall happen now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:37:45-07:00","id":957161,"title":"","content":"Well, helping Friend Claim someone is not likely to earn LJ many friends, I'd wager. Kinda hoping she has to try and explain her new rhyme-favouring Friend to her other, fleshy friends at some point. I'm sure that'd go down <i>fantastically</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/704-edge","name":"Edge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar704_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:37:20-07:00","id":957285,"title":"","content":"Friend is my favorite spirit I've ever portrayed. So alien and distant - there is a lot of lucidity in what he says...if you can read his vocabulary, which I suspect most can't. To bring him into the Flesh Realm has very big implications - it shows how LJ is so removed from the Oath of the Moon, how independently she's going it...and the intense pull in multiple directions she must feel. She insists that she is good and that she wants to show the Compact that she isn't a monster, yet here is her terror-god ally requesting that she let him claim a body.<br /> <br /> Choices choices LJ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:39:19-07:00","id":957286,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a big metal body sitting right there...<br /> <br /> (Have I mentioned that I love this AP? I love this AP. I check it every damn day to see if there's an update. And when there is my productivity at work takes one helluva hit...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:26:43-07:00","id":957511,"title":"","content":"Wow thank you, I'm humbled by your praise. <br /> <br /> There is, indeed, a metal body, but Friend might have particular demands for what he shall clothe himself in, and LJ had a vision for Honeybun i think.<br /> <br /> Thanks for staying with us even through our being slow. We're gonna play more this Saturday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T05:02:57-07:00","id":957525,"title":"","content":"Also, if ye like my AP, please give us a rating you think we deserve on RPG.net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:06:43-07:00","id":958014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=957511#post957511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow thank you, I'm humbled by your praise.<br /> <br /> There is, indeed, a metal body, but Friend might have particular demands for what he shall clothe himself in, and LJ had a vision for Honeybun i think.<br /> <br /> Thanks for staying with us even through our being slow. We're gonna play more this Saturday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, I did figure that would be unlikely based both on the nascent characterisation of the golem not matching Friend's persona and that, well, the alternative has more potential for Drama(TM).<br /> <br /> Look forward to reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T00:57:29-08:00","id":1055123,"title":"","content":"Been a while - posting more of my AP!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:47:36-08:00","id":1059045,"title":"","content":"Slightly belated, as I had to find a chance to catch up, but it's great to see some more from LJ and co! I am thoroughly intrigued and and stumped by the nature of the Ambitious One, the Sea and the Grindylows - really eager to see if this little quest is going to be as much of a trainwreck as I fear, or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:38:13-08:00","id":1059067,"title":"","content":"Sounded like a Changeling thing to me, to be honest. Hard to tell, though, with the information Lilith has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:08:46-07:00","id":1062527,"title":"","content":"Errol, I wouldn't say you're too far off. I drew a great deal of inspiration from Changeling HOWEVER - not all Supernaturals in WoD exist in a fashion that LJ would meet them. Most, I'd say, I simply don't use. Changeling likely won't make any appearances, definitely out are (new) Demon, Promethean, Beasts, Mummies, Sin-Eaters, and other minor ones I can't remember. Confirmed existing are Vampires (I lean toward nWoDizing Masquerade), Hunters...And there are other beings in there. There may be things from Dragon: the Coil if LJ ever happens upon them.<br /> <br /> Posting more tonight. Come one come all and feast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:03:16-07:00","id":1062597,"title":"","content":"More Seventh Seal posted. More to come!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:34:49-07:00","id":1076512,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, loving the story so far. Permission to steal liberally from this for my home game? I too have difficulty figuring out how to deal with spirits, but when playing with you I never really got that impression. I must say your efforts here have paid off in quality. Well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:02:11-07:00","id":1077830,"title":"","content":"Hail to thee, yes of course you may steal. Go ahead and use it as inspiration if you wish, twist as you please. Enjoy, and thanks for asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T09:33:44-07:00","id":1085059,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2 is ended. More to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T19:50:14-07:00","id":1086961,"title":"","content":"Quick note to deliver accolades: your writing is excellent and the characterization is especially strong. I'm grateful for the strong presentation of spirits and the Hisil, as that's an area I've struggled with, personally. Makes me wonder a bit, however, if the way LJ treats them partially explains their humanity--in a &quot;rubbing off&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T08:55:33-07:00","id":1087189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=1086961#post1086961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick note to deliver accolades: your writing is excellent and the characterization is especially strong. I'm grateful for the strong presentation of spirits and the Hisil, as that's an area I've struggled with, personally. Makes me wonder a bit, however, if the way LJ treats them partially explains their humanity--in a &quot;rubbing off&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well well well! Somebody noticed this! Color me pleased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> yes. The way that LJ treats them humanizes them, but it's also a matter of perspective that I've been able to express because this is a solo game. To those Wolves who are very comfortable with spirits and are deeply set in their humanity, like LJ is, the spirits they interact with regularly will start to interact with them in a way that is highly relatable. Now an Uratha who is comfortable with spirits but who lives in a forested territory, lives mostly as a wolf and views the world in terms of 'wolf' sensibilities will find the spirits interacting with them in a way more focused on their wolven nature - less ambiguous, more 'natural', much more predator-prey focus. Spirits are highly malleable, impressionable things, and as quantum mechanics seems influenced by observers, Hisil mechanics are influenced by interactors.<br /> <br /> Thank you, by the way, for your kind words, it is deeply flattering to both Shopping and myself and very rewarding to know that people are enjoying our game. I just got done moving, so we're gonna start back up and deliver some more game. What's going to come next? LJ has met The Old Man...What lies ahead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:05:13-07:00","id":1087272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=1087189#post1087189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well well well! Somebody noticed this! Color me pleased <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> yes. The way that LJ treats them humanizes them, but it's also a matter of perspective that I've been able to express because this is a solo game. To those Wolves who are very comfortable with spirits and are deeply set in their humanity, like LJ is, the spirits they interact with regularly will start to interact with them in a way that is highly relatable. Now an Uratha who is comfortable with spirits but who lives in a forested territory, lives mostly as a wolf and views the world in terms of 'wolf' sensibilities will find the spirits interacting with them in a way more focused on their wolven nature - less ambiguous, more 'natural', much more predator-prey focus. <b>Spirits are highly malleable, impressionable things, and as quantum mechanics seems influenced by observers, Hisil mechanics are influenced by interactors.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an astute observation, and a bit of distilled Hisil wisdom worth savoring for its application in-game. Makes spirits (the by-far #1 most viscerally terrifying element of the CofD, to me) more handle-able as a Storyteller. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you, by the way, for your kind words, it is deeply flattering to both Shopping and myself and very rewarding to know that people are enjoying our game. I just got done moving, so we're gonna start back up and deliver some more game. What's going to come next? LJ has met The Old Man...What lies ahead? </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to it. You and Shopping are spending a lot of time on smaller interactions that help to pull the character along as a person, and that's commendable. It also shows off the characterization, in particular you've done well and practiced something many find very hard: showing (rather than telling) characters as angry, emotional and unstable people--deeply wounded and unhinged.<br /> <br /> Also sensing a big dose of Fallen London in the current threads.... Anyway, inspiring to see good work and may nudge me to put an old campaign up sooner or later.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T14:53:53-07:00","id":1087343,"title":"","content":"Thanks Khanwulf. A lot of the credit goes to my dear friend, fellow gamer, and ST Aynie. She helped drive home the idea of perspective for me, and it influenced how I view spirit interactions.<br /> <br /> More to come my astute friends! LJ prepares to go into the Sea Beneath while handling troubles above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T13:08:47-07:00","id":1106707,"title":"","content":"Greetings delicious friends.<br /> <br /> More Seventh Seal posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T17:25:50-07:00","id":1123244,"title":"","content":"Even -more- Seventh Seal!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T10:36:26-07:00","id":1123543,"title":"","content":"Awesome! <br /> <br /> And... hurr.. that shofar?! Well done. I may have to borrow that idea later (much later) for Dark Eras play. When I need an apocalyptic McGuffin. That's suckers got history streaming off it.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T13:45:17-07:00","id":1123618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=1123543#post1123543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome! <br /> <br /> And... hurr.. that shofar?! Well done. I may have to borrow that idea later (much later) for Dark Eras play. When I need an apocalyptic McGuffin. That's suckers got history streaming off it.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, I'm glad you like it. The Shofar, the Amulet, the Torah...all quite powerful in their own right. The Shofar is the most obvious of them. It, like the Old Man, has a lot of history surrounding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T00:14:02-07:00","id":1128350,"title":"","content":"Come one, come all - LJ has finally marshaled the power of her spirit, gathered enough Ulal, and rolled some good rolls...and she's destroyed the massive pillar of ice that was hanging out in the library! Check out the log to see what she discovered beneath <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T11:50:36-07:00","id":1152856,"title":"","content":"Friend knows...that it's been too long since we've had an update! More has been posted, along with a dramatic battle between LJ and a mysterious other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T11:52:19-07:00","id":1152858,"title":"","content":"ugh, posted twice by mistake, won't let me delete...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3028,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","user":"viskarenvisla","date":". 10-25-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T09:21:06-08:00","id":1179850,"title":"","content":"<i>Svagatam, Konnichiwa, M'bharav</i> my friends.<br /> <br /> Another exciting post in Seventh Seal has been made - it has been some time, but I have caught up with being an adult, and now I offer you a glimpse into the Dark...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T22:05:58-08:00","id":1181911,"title":"","content":"So. For those of you who have caught up to where we are, knowing now the identity of the great Shadow that hangs over Chicago, what would you do in LJ's shoes? Use spoiler tags if necessary, although I can't say I was too creative in this choice ultimately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T01:13:38-08:00","id":1181940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viskarenvisla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/830599-presenting-my-werewolf-ap-the-seventh-seal?p=1181911#post1181911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. For those of you who have caught up to where we are, knowing now the identity of the great Shadow that hangs over Chicago, what would you do in LJ's shoes? Use spoiler tags if necessary, although I can't say I was too creative in this choice ultimately.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some situations in our last game are weirdly parallel with yours in places, though mine trailed off ages ago and my character was very different.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">As LJ, and I have no idea how I'd do it, but I'd set up some safeguards before letting the Sheddai know, and ensure they know the possible repercussions of it, because the Shofar falling into Olivia's hands would be a big win for her. I'd also want Agonistes to know (I know he's there but he might not have made out what was said), because I wouldn't want to be dragged through the wringer again and it's time someone else deal with it, even though it would lead to more horrible things later (though I like him, as a character). But I'm not playing the hero.<br /> <br /> In our first game we did an exorcism, some kid, a friend of one of the packs little sister, who was possessed by a murder spirit. It was horrible, and all the worse because it was sort of spontaneous. The moment we realized what was going on we jumped into action, even if it involved holding this puny teenage kid to the ground while he screamed and begged and lied, then ripping out the thing infesting his soul. Sometimes you have to do what you have to do.<br /> <br /> As for the reveal, I liked it. It was less an 'oh shit' and more of an 'oh yes!'. I'm a fan of the Chicago book, and she is probably my favorite werewolf NPC, so while she'd been mentioned a couple times before I didn't think she'd actually make more of a presence and was glad that it looks like she is, and she's making a big one.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}